# The payload: an AAR of ~14 MB (two ABIs) plus the staged tree it is zipped from
# and the notice file generated beside it. Built by
# scripts/build-gi-runtime-android.mjs against an Android GI stack, never
# committed — the same arrangement as the gtk-runtime-* bundles' `gtk/`.
platforms/*
stage/

# EXCEPT the gradle hook, which is hand-written and MUST travel in the checkout.
# It is the only thing that can fail loudly when the payload above was never
# built: NativeScript applies it from the same directory it scans for `*.aar`,
# so a locally linked checkout without a built AAR stops the app's gradle run by
# name instead of producing an APK that dies in dlopen at startup.
!platforms/android/
platforms/android/*
!platforms/android/include.gradle
